# `git archive` substitutes the commit into this file, so a build from a source
# tarball can still name the commit it came from. Without it the version command
# in src/meson.build finds no .git, `git rev-parse` prints nothing, and
# `git diff --quiet` fails -- producing the banner "platterpus-fork-g-dirty",
# which names no build at all AND falsely claims the tree was modified. Every
# logfile records that string permanently, so a rip from such a build is
# unusable as evidence. Found while packaging beta.7 for the rig.
/src/archive-version.txt export-subst

# Line endings (review C item 6.6). Every text file is LF in the repository,
# and is checked out LF on every platform, whatever core.autocrlf says: the
# Windows job checks this tree out, and a CRLF copy of a CUE sheet, a golden
# log or a shell script is a different file to whatever reads it. git judges
# which files are text.
* text=auto eol=lf
# Kept byte for byte. A fuzz seed may hold a CR on purpose, and the evidence
# copies are checked against SHA-256s of their sources.
/tests/fuzz/seeds/** -text
/tests/fixtures/evidence/** -text
